  "type": "Manifest",
  "label": {
    "en": [
      "A vintage postal card with Russian imperial printing. At the top in red Cyrillic letters it reads 'ПОЧТОВАЯ КАРТОЧКА' and bears a red Imperial Russian coat of arms and a red 3-kopek stamp with double-headed eagle. There are circular postmarks and handwritten address text, partly in Latin script (Estonian) and partly in Cyrillic, including references to Tallinn/Reval."
    ]
  },
